{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamilyExclusions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamilyExclusions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.not_powerLaw_of_log_ratios_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.not_powerLaw_of_log_ratios_differ","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L122-L133","doc":"**The exclusion.** If the exponent extracted across one scale factor differs\nfrom the exponent extracted across another, no single `p` — and hence no pure\npower law `c · x^p` — reproduces both. Stated as the contrapositive of\n`powerLaw_log_ratio` applied at two base points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.powerLaw_log_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.powerLaw_log_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L110-L120","doc":"**A pure power law has a scale-invariant log-ratio.** For `Φ x = c · x^p` the\nquantity `log Φ(k·x) − log Φ(x)` is `p · log k` — it depends on the scale factor\n`k` alone and not on where along the ray it is measured. That is the identity the\nthree-point grid tests twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_ne_zero_example","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_ne_zero_example","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L101-L106","doc":"**The test has teeth.** A grid on which the determinant is nonzero exists, so\n`not_realizable_of_det3_ne_zero` has non-empty hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_eq_zero_of_construction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_eq_zero_of_construction","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** The determinant does vanish on data that *is* realizable, so\nthe test is not excluding everything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.not_realizable_of_det3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.not_realizable_of_det3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**The exclusion, as a candidate filter.** A nonzero determinant rules out the\nentire two-parameter family for that shape `ψ` — every `(c, a)` simultaneously,\nwith nothing fitted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_eq_zero_of_realizable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3_eq_zero_of_realizable","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L79-L87","doc":"**Realizability forces the determinant to vanish.** If the data is a linear\ncombination of the two shape columns then the three columns are dependent. No\nhypothesis on `x` or `ψ` is needed — in particular the grid need not be\nincreasing and the shapes need not be independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.det3","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The `3 × 3` determinant of the columns `(x, ψ, φ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.Realizable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AggregatorFamily.Realizable","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AggregatorFamilyExclusions.lean#L68-L71","doc":"The data `φ` is realizable on the grid `x` by the two-parameter family\n`c·x + a·ψ` for **some** choice of the two parameters. ","signatureChunk":0}]}